        {
          "text": "CH'ÊN Ch'i-yüan 陳啟源 (T. 長發, H. 見桃居士), d. 1689, scholar, was a native of Wu-chiang, Kiangsu, and a close friend of Chu Ho-ling 朱鶴齡 (T. 長孺, H. 愚菴, 1606–1683) of the same locality. A licentiate, he collaborated with the latter in the compilation of a comprehensive study of the Odes, entitled 毛詩通義 Mao-shih t'ung-i, in 12 chüan, which is regarded as inferior to his own critical study of the Odes based on the exposition of pre-T'ang scholars.",
